    "body": "> Is the tab or newline check needed? It seems simpler to just check for `<`\r\n\r\nThis change follows the same logic as previous [dangling markup injection mitigation](https://chromestatus.com/feature/5735596811091968). If we were to only check for `<`, we have to change the use counter in Chromium to see if that's compatible first.",
