    "created_at": "2023-05-30T18:54:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-30T18:54:00Z",
    "body": "> You also forgot about the `formtarget` attribute. We probably want to restructure \"get an element's target\" to make that less likely going forward. Perhaps it should take a target value as argument as well and in that case only the validation happens.\r\n\r\nSince `formtarget` must have [values that are valid navigable target names or keywords](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#attributes-for-form-submission:~:text=The%20target%20and%20formtarget%20content%20attributes%2C%20if%20specified%2C%20must%20have%20values%20that%20are%20valid%20navigable%20target%20names%20or%20keywords.), I think that should be covered by the change we are making to the [valid navigable target name](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#valid-navigable-target-name)?\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
